# * help command
# The help command shows documentation, dispatching on its first argument.

# ** 1. Bare help shows the quick reference card (like plain hledger).
$ hledger help
> /HLEDGER QUICK REFERENCE/

# ** 2. help commands shows the commands list.
$ hledger help commands
> /Commands \(including installed/

# ** 3. help usage shows general command-line usage.
$ hledger help usage
> /hledger's main command line interface/

# ** 4. help usage CMD shows that command's usage.
$ hledger help usage balance
> /^balance \[OPTIONS\]/

# ** 5. help manual TOPIC shows the manual.
$ hledger help manual journal
> /hledger User Manuals/

# ** 6. An unrecognised help argument is treated as a manual topic.
$ hledger help journal
> /hledger User Manuals/

# ** 7. A manual topic matching no heading shows a note (not an error, and not the manual).
$ hledger help nosuchtopic
>2 /does not match any section heading in the hledger manual/

# ** 8. A unique case-insensitive prefix of a heading resolves to that section.
$ hledger help "text enc"
> /hledger User Manuals/

# ** 9. A unique infix (substring) match resolves to that section.
$ hledger help periods
> /hledger User Manuals/

# ** 10. An ambiguous topic (matching several headings) lists them, so one can be chosen.
$ hledger help Text
> /matches several manual sections/

# ** 11. A multi-word TOPIC must be quoted.
$ hledger help 'time periods'
> /hledger User Manuals/

# ** 12. The empty topic lists all manual topics.
$ hledger help ''
> /hledger manual topics:/

# ** 13. help manual with no topic lists all manual topics.
$ hledger help manual
> /hledger manual topics:/

# ** 14. The manual title (HLEDGER, with the (1) stripped) can be matched.
$ hledger help hledger
> /hledger User Manuals/

# ** 15. help -l TOPIC just lists the matching topics (instead of showing the manual).
$ hledger help -l text
>
hledger manual topics matching "text":
  Text encoding
  Text output

# ** 16. help examples errors clearly when a command has no examples.
$ hledger help examples nosuchcommand
>2 /there are no examples for hledger-nosuchcommand/
>=1

# ** 17. help quickref shows the quick reference card.
$ hledger help quickref
> /HLEDGER QUICK REFERENCE/

# ** 18. help commands --builtin shows only built-in commands.
$ hledger help commands --builtin
> /Commands \(showing built-in/
